Sensitivity of HFET2 devices (#164)
* HFET2 (z level 6, hfet2/hfet2*.c) under .sens: a shared n-channel model with
* two instances (one at dtemp=10) in parallel across the sensed supply, and a
* p-channel at temp=50 whose drain current returns through that same supply, so
* every device's columns reach the sensed current. The output is the drain
* current rather than a gate node, because sensing a ~1 uV gate node pays for
* it with cancellation-limited rows (see sens_mesa).
*
* Three C behaviours the replay reproduces:
* - d2 and eta2 are ordinary values but their *given* flags gate
*   hfet2load.c's nsc branch (hfet2temp.c fills N02 under eta2Given alone) and
*   the walk never clears a flag, so a card that gave only one of them would
*   report a topology jump instead of a derivative for those two rows.
* - hfet2ask.c answers the instance temperature in Celsius while hfet2param.c
*   stores it in kelvin.
* - HFET2_VT1/VT2 follow the raw VTO, not the type-scaled TVTO, so the
*   p-channel's thresholds stay negative while its TVTO is positive.
.options reltol=1e-10 vntol=1e-13 abstol=1e-16
vds 1 0 dc 2.0
vids 1 2 dc 0
vgs 4 0 dc 0.5
rg 4 3 1k
vgs2 8 0 dc 1.8
rg2 8 7 1k
z1 2 3 0 nmos l=1u w=20u
z2 2 3 0 nmos l=2u w=40u dtemp=10
z3 0 7 2 pmos l=1u w=20u temp=50
.model nmos nhfet level=6 eta2=2 d2=0.3e-6 rd=20 rs=30 rdi=5 rsi=7
.model pmos phfet level=6 eta2=2 d2=0.3e-6 rd=20 rs=30
.sens i(vids)
.end
